<title>MALTA: Malta issues 15 million lira of government bonds.</title>
<headline>Malta issues 15 million lira of government bonds.</headline>
<dateline>VALLETTA 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Maltese government said it plans two issues of government bonds totalling 15 million lira ($43 million) to fund part of its 1996 deficit.</p>
<p>One issue of 12 million lira carries a coupon of 7.5 percent interest and is redeemable in 2011. The other 3 million lira issue pays 6.3 percent and is redeemable in 1999.</p>
<p>Applications for multiples of 100 lira can be made between September 23 and 28. The bonds will be traded on the Malta stock exchange.</p>
<p>($=0.36 Maltese lira)</p>
</text>
